content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-101 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22120, filtered-water line (sodium hypochlorite dosed)",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 3.0 mm/s against the HF-300 Figure 3 severity zones (mm/s RMS, measured on bearing housings): this is Zone B (2.8–4.5, 'Long-term operation'). It is above Zone A (new machines, up to 2.8), below the Zone C boundary of 4.5 (plan maintenance) and well below the Zone D boundary of 7.1 (stop the pump). The reading is acceptable, so no stop is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone (Zone D, 7.1 mm/s and above). The site rule to stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer is therefore not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 69 C against the manual limits (normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C): this is within the normal band but only 1 C below its upper limit. It is below the alarm limit, so the site priority-1 rule (temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit) is not triggered.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Dry-run event of about 15 minutes against the manual requirement (seal flush Plan 11 from pump discharge, 'never run dry'): the operating limit was violated. The troubleshooting table lists 'seal run dry' as a cause of shaft-seal leakage. No leakage is visible yet, but seal face damage is likely.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal faces overheated or damaged by about 15 minutes of dry running (loss of Plan 11 flush). This is the most likely latent defect, even though no leakage is visible yet.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration of 3.0 mm/s (Zone B) may reflect damage from the dry-run or changeover event. Documented causes of high vibration are misalignment, bearing wear, impeller imbalance or damage, and cavitation. Air drawn into the suction during the tank changeover is a possible contributor.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature near the top of the normal band (69 C, limit 70 C). Documented causes of high bearing temperature are over-greasing, bearing wear and misalignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Before shutdown, increase monitoring. Measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading against Figure 3. Record housing temperature and check the seal for leakage each shift until the seal is replaced.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Escalate if limits are reached. If vibration reaches Zone D (7.1 mm/s or more), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart. If housing temperature exceeds 80 C, raise to P1 within the shift (trip is at 90 C). If seal leakage appears, bring the seal replacement forward.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Plan the planned seal replacement (manual 5.2, as modified by SB-2026-014). Obtain the LOTO, mechanical isolation and line-break permits, and a signed lifting plan. Then isolate the pump, drain it and vent it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using certified lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the impeller nut and impeller. Inspect the impeller for damage as part of investigating the vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Withdraw the seal and sleeve. Inspect the sleeve for scoring and replace sleeve HF3-455 if the scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect the bearings. If either bearing shows wear, noise or evidence of high temperature, replace both bearings as a pair (manual 5.3).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit cartridge seal HF3-450B. Do NOT fit HF3-450. The HF3-450B is pre-set, so no sleeve setting measurement is needed. Fit a new casing gasket.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm, per SB-2026-014; this supersedes the 25 Nm in Table 5.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Tighten the remaining fasteners to Table 5 (lightly oiled threads): impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm, bearing housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm, casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the motor or bearing housing was moved, laser-align the shaft. Tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm the pump is fully primed and the Plan 11 seal flush is established; never run the pump dry. After restart, record vibration on both bearing housings against Figure 3, record housing temperature against the 70/80/90 C limits, and check the seal for leakage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal (supersedes HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "Not given in evidence",
      "description": "Casing gasket, new one required at each seal replacement",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency item: fit only if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out (LOTO) at the MCC before any work inside the pump or on its seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical isolation of the suction and discharge valves.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Line-break permit, with the pump drained and vented first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment, because the back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg (more than 25 kg).",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves, because P-101 is on a sodium hypochlorite dosed line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If vibration reaches the highest severity zone (Zone D, 7.1 mm/s or more), stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement: 4.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, if the motor or bearing housing is moved: 1.5 h with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Contingency, only if the bearings are found worn: bearing pair replacement, 6.0 h with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal part. The manual procedure 5.2 and Table 5 cover the original seal HF3-450. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) says HF3-450 must not be fitted on serial HF3-22000 and above, and HF3-450B must be used instead. P-101 is serial HF3-22120, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies and HF3-450B is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque. Manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm (M10); SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. The bulletin applies to serial HF3-22120 and the HF3-450B seal, so use 30 Nm. All other Table 5 torques are not changed by the bulletin and still apply.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling. The manual says to inspect the sleeve for scoring. The bulletin adds that HF3-450B needs no sleeve measurement, and that sleeve HF3-455 must be replaced if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm. Both apply to this pump, and the bulletin's 0.1 mm criterion is used.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The report does not say whether 3.0 mm/s is an RMS reading, which bearing housing it was taken on, or whether both housings were measured, as section 3 requires.",
    "There is no baseline vibration or temperature trend for P-101, so it is unknown whether 3.0 mm/s and 69 C are increases caused by the dry run.",
    "The evidence gives no criterion for deciding between pre-emptive seal replacement and running until leakage appears after a dry-run event. P2 planned replacement is a planning judgement, and the site's P2/P3 definitions are not given.",
    "The casing gasket part number is not given; the exploded view (Figure 2) has callout numbers but no parts list or names.",
    "The evidence does not say whether removing the back pull-out assembly moves the bearing housing enough to require laser alignment. The planner should confirm this.",
    "The evidence does not state any allowable dry-run duration or a specific inspection required after dry running.",
    "Bearing part numbers and grease quantity or specification are not given, if bearing replacement or a grease check is needed.",
    "It is not stated which bearing housing the 69 C temperature was measured on."
  ]
}
